Expected elements: present

Presence check passes on every item. The fixed nav sits above a body that clears it; the provenance banner is in the content column, left-aligned with the breadcrumb, affirmative green, `Real Aztec mainnet data` beside `aztec-mainnet`, with the producer's sentences below. The `Not observable` badge carries the published pruning reason and locates it in the chain's retention. The full hash, `Succeeded` badge and a four-row Overview are all present. Internal calls and State changes both say "empty permanently, not yet". Footer closes the page; the disclosure does not claim demo data; heart, CodeTracer mark and GitHub mark are all drawn and visible. Nothing forbidden appears — no retry, no spinner, no trace reference, no danger tone.

The weakest element is the value cell of the last Overview row, COST · TRANSACTIONFEE. The dangling separator is gone, but what remains is worse than the separator ever was: the page's only quantity is rendered as a 66-character zero-padded hex word whose 47 leading zeros consume the full data column, pushing the sixteen significant digits to the far right edge before `mana (FeeJuice)`. A reader cannot tell the order of magnitude of the fee, which is the only question this row exists to answer. It is also the only double-height row in the table, because the flattened all-caps label wraps. Rubric A5 asks for tabular figures and truncation at meaningful boundaries; a cost printed as an address fails both.

Highest-priority fix: render the fee as a decimal mana amount, keeping the raw word available on demand.

